                <pb facs="0246" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11010: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-21T17:00:00+08:00">July 21, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 21—9:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>600. Following from American Consul [General] at Shanghai: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 15, 3 p.m. In vicinity of Soochow, Standard Oil Company launch <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Mei Foo II</hi> was held up by bandits on July 9
                            at 6 p.m. and all that was worth while was looted. One foreigner
                            received slight injury but was permitted to continue. Chinese
                            authorities have been requested to make investigation and punish those
                            guilty of the offense and to take such precautionary measures as are
                            necessary to protect life in this large commercial district. This
                            incident is reported to the Legation as illustrating degree of
                            protection which is afforded by National Government in the district
                            where it has undisputed control. The bandits threaten that should the
                            incident be given publicity <pb facs="0247" n="149" xml:id="pg149"/>
                            through the press all Standard Oil Company boats will be captured when
                            plying between Shanghai and Soochow.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
